 "attribution": "Film look data derived from spektrafilm by Andrea Volpato, https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm. Licensed CC BY-SA 4.0. Modified: fitted to the Olympus E-PM2's adjustable stages. See NOTICE.md.",
 "description": "The black-and-white film Kodak Double-X 5222 (black-and-white negative, on Kodak 2302 print film) in the menu entry Grainy Film. The entry keeps its stored value and its art codes 74 and 83: the firmware makes the picture monochrome and runs its grain program as before. The spec adds a third part to the art-matrix chain, with the matrix behind it (how colours turn into grey), and writes the contrast table of the grain program (the tone of still pictures) and the look table of the two codes for live view and movies. A delta on the structure spec of the twelve-film build: it changes the last jump of that spec's chain. Leave the entry spec of Grainy Film out of the build. Grainy Film II is not changed.",
